        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "> Thanks for the PR!\r\n> \r\n> Could you, please, elaborate on why you think this is needed?\r\n\r\nFor example, help window of nvim-tree is a scratch buffer, and ignore all autocmd to open_win, so I cannot disable indentscope through autocmd.\r\n\r\n<img width=\"288\" alt=\"Xnip2025-02-05_12-46-14\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/dc1f8671-b997-4779-9b7c-ee4dea82c4db\" />\r\n\r\nAccording to the original implementation, to disable indentscope in a specific buffer, only the blacklist method can be used (by setting b:miniindentscope_disable=true). It is difficult to achieve under the above circumstances.\r\n\r\nSo I want to enable indentscope by using the whitelist. To achieve this function, it is only necessary to modify the global and local usage logic of the `miniindentscope_disable` variable to be consistent with the behavior of neovim.\r\n\r\nAnd still be able to retain the original blacklist-like working method.",
            "created_at": "2025-02-05T04:53:11Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/pull/1552#issuecomment-2635699544",
            "id": 2635699544,
            "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/1552",
            "minimized": null,
            "node_id": "IC_kwDOFoksYM6dGZVY",
            "performed_via_github_app": null,
            "reactions": {
