        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> The essence is that the `mini.indentscope` plugin generally works in normal buffers, which will set basic information such as filetype, and for those scratch buffers (which often have many strange behaviors, such as no filetype, ignoring all autocmds), `b:miniindentscope_disable` must be set to be disabled, which is quite difficult to achieve in practice.\r\n\r\nScratch buffers can be identified by checking 'buftype' option. And if they block autocommands from executing, then changing the behavior won't make it easier for automated disabling.\r\n\r\n> Therefore, I think it is necessary to modify the working method of this variable to be consistent with the local option behavior of neovim.\r\n\r\nAs was said in previous comment, any solution that can be done with this PR's suggested approach can be rewritten in the current approach. Although being consistent with how local buffer options work is good, it was (and is) not the goal here.",
